 "Gender dysphoria is the distress some transgender and gender-diverse people feel when their inner sense of gender doesn't match their body or the sex recorded at birth, and the way others treat them because of it. Being transgender is not a disorder. The diagnosis describes the distress, and exists mainly so people can get care. Not every trans person has dysphoria, and the distress usually eases when a person can live as themselves with support and, when wanted, medical care.",
